Applied Machine Learning (COMP3132)

This repository contains assignments from my Applied Machine Learning course, focusing on neural networks, image processing, and model evaluation using Python.


OVERVIEW

These projects demonstrate hands-on experience with:
    - Data preprocessing and dataset handling
    - Neural networks and deep learning concepts
    - Image classification and convolution operations
    - Model evaluation, overfitting, and performance improvement techniques


TECHNOLOGIES
    - Python
    - NumPy, Pandas
    - Matplotlib
    - TensorFlow / Keras
    - Jupyter Notebook


ASSIGNMENTS
Assignment 1 – MNIST vs Fashion-MNIST Analysis
    - Compared performance between MNIST and Fashion-MNIST datasets
    - Analyzed classification difficulty and accuracy differences
    - Explored how dataset complexity affects model performance

Assignment 2 – Iris Classification (Neural Networks)
    - Built a multiclass classification model using the Iris dataset
    - Converted categorical labels into numerical format
    - Explored model architecture (layers, neurons) and overfitting
    - Evaluated model performance and generalization

Assignment 3 – Convolution & Neural Networks
    - Implemented and visualized 2D convolution operations
    - Applied kernels for edge and line detection in images
    - Trained a neural network for image-related tasks
    - Developed understanding of feature extraction in CNNs

Assignment 4 – CIFAR-10 & Overfitting Reduction
    - Built a convolutional neural network (CNN) on CIFAR-10
    - Demonstrated overfitting using an overparameterized model
    - Applied techniques to improve performance:
    - Dropout
    - L2 Regularization
    - Data Augmentation
    - Compared model performance using loss and accuracy graphs

KEY TAKEAWAYS
    - Strong understanding of deep learning fundamentals
    - Experience working with image datasets and CNNs
    - Ability to identify and reduce overfitting in models
    - Practical knowledge of the full ML workflow (data → model → evaluation)